# Process definitions for Procfile-reading platforms. Railway (Nixpacks) reads
# the `release:` line but not the others; see docs/deploy-railway.md for where
# each of these goes in that dashboard.
#
# There is deliberately NO `web:` line. The one that used to be here called
# vendor/bin/heroku-php-apache2, a binary supplied by Heroku's PHP buildpack —
# nothing in composer.json installs it, so it existed on exactly zero of the
# platforms this app was going to. With no web line, Nixpacks supplies its own
# nginx + php-fpm and serves public/ correctly.
#
# There is also no `worker:` line any more. routes/console.php schedules one
# command, daily, and app/ dispatches no queued jobs at all, so an always-on
# worker process would bill full-time to run sanctum:prune-expired once a day.
# Use the platform's cron feature instead.
release: php artisan config:cache && php artisan route:cache && php artisan migrate --force && php artisan storage:link
